# plans/BUILD_AND_DEPENDENCY_SYSTEM_REDESIGN.md §4.6: a workspace root declares
# its members and `yo build -p <name>` builds one of them.
#
# The fixture exercises both member-pattern forms at once: `packages/*` is a
# glob (matching `core` and `app`) and `examples/demo` is a literal. `-p app`
# names the member by its `[package] name`, not its directory — that is what a
# member is called everywhere else (`import("name")`, `build.dependency("name")`).
#
# What this pins: the member's build file is what runs. The root's own build.yo
# defines only a do-nothing `install`, so if `-p` were ignored the summary would
# come from the root and no artifact would be built. Only the summary line is
# compared — the child compile's chatter carries machine-specific paths.
timeout=900
stdout_keep_match=Build Summary: [0-9]+/[0-9]+ steps succeeded
